EXERCISED PATH: model/layers.py:169-183 -> model/model.py:87-94 -> train_rqvae.py:432-453 | Traced the backward pass: `quant_loss = beta*(weights*commitment).mean() + mse(x, x_q.detach())` (layers.py:177-178) is the only loss term of the level, `commitment` is `poincare_distance(point, code.detach())**2` with `point = clamp_ball(exp_0(latent))` differentiable in the encoder, so a real gradient reaches the encoder and decoder; the codebook takes no gradient by design (layers.py:84 `requires_grad_(False)`), which is also what makes `find_unused_parameters=False` DDP safe. Numerics: every point is clamped to radius 1-1e-4 (`clamp_ball`), every `atanh` argument to 1-1e-7 in float64 (frechet_poincare.py:97-98,77,84), every denominator `clamp_min(1e-12)`, and `apply` drops non-finite slots (`torch.isfinite`, 197-199) — no inf/nan path found in float32. Switching `use_behaviour` off makes the weights all-ones and switching `use_curvature` off replaces distance, commitment and the codebook step with Euclidean ones, i.e. the coupled pathway measurably changes assignment, commit gradient and slot positions in each configuration.
