FINDING SEVERITY: blocking
FINDING LOCATION: train_rqvae.py:49-59
FINDING DETAIL: `_repository_root` returns the first ancestor `p` for which `(p / "stage2_RQ-VAE").is_dir()`, and RESULT_DIR is then built as `REPO_ROOT / "results" / "stage2_RQ-VAE" / ARM_NAME`. The directory `results/stage2_RQ-VAE` exists (it is the mandated result directory), so the first match walking up is the `results` directory itself, not the repository root: REPO_ROOT resolves to `<repo>/results`. Consequently EMBEDDING_FILE becomes `<repo>/results/stage1_GeneEmbedding/output/sentence_t5.npy`, TRAIN_FILE becomes `<repo>/results/results/stage0_build_parquet/train.parquet` and RESULT_DIR becomes `<repo>/results/results/stage2_RQ-VAE/TIGER_poincare-frechet-successor-codebook`. The trainer therefore cannot even read its inputs (`load_embeddings` raises at train_rqvae.py:317) and, if it did, would write its SID outside the mandated `results/stage2_RQ-VAE/<promoted tree name>/`, where admission and the Stage 3 trainer look for `item_sids.json`. The same resolution happens both from the round tree and from the promoted `results/stage2_RQ-VAE/<arm>/` location, so promotion does not repair it. The docstring's claim that the marker "differs between the two locations while the number of parents does" is precisely what fails, because the marker is the same directory the file is later copied next to.
FINDING REPRODUCTION: With the real layout `<repo>/results/stage2_RQ-VAE/...` and the file at `<repo>/results/stage2_RQ-VAE/<arm>/train_rqvae.py` or at `.../trees/round_*/<tree>/train_rqvae.py`, iterate `Path(__file__).resolve().parents`: the first `p` with `p/"stage2_RQ-VAE"` a directory is `<repo>/results`; print the returned root or simply `python -c` the two-line loop — it yields `<repo>/results`, so `TRAIN_FILE` is `<repo>/results/results/stage0_build_parquet/train.parquet`. Any run then dies at train_rqvae.py:317 with FileNotFoundError (or, at best, writes into `<repo>/results/results/stage2_RQ-VAE/...`).
FINDING CORRECTION: Match the marker one level down and return the root that contains it, e.g. `for parent in here.parents: if (parent / "results" / "stage2_RQ-VAE").is_dir(): return parent`, leaving RESULT_DIR as `REPO_ROOT/"results"/"stage2_RQ-VAE"/ARM_NAME`; alternatively return `parent` and build RESULT_DIR without the extra `"results"` join. Anchor the search so the tree copy and the promoted copy resolve to the same repository root, and assert at start-up that EMBEDDING_FILE and TRAIN_FILE exist before any GPU work.